&nbsp;&nbsp;Independent confirmation of acceleration. Together with Riess et al., these papers anchor the essayâ€™s cosmological arc.</li>
<li class="break-words">Dodelson, S. (2003). Modern Cosmology. Academic Press.
&nbsp;&nbsp;Textbook treatment of cosmological models. Offers mathematical structure (FRW metrics, Î›CDM parameters) that contextualizes why isotropy/homogeneity constrain external universes â€” supporting your claim that â€œthe universe doesnâ€™t try all parameters.â€</li>
<li class="break-words">Whittle, M. (2006). The Cosmic Symphony: The Universe Revealed. Cambridge University Press.
&nbsp;&nbsp;Accessible overview of modern cosmology, focusing on energy flows and cosmic history. Useful for connecting thermodynamic analogies to cosmic dynamics.</li>
<li class="break-words">Whittle, M. (2015). Cosmology (ASTR 1230, University of Virginia). Lecture 12: â€œFalling Outward.â€
&nbsp;&nbsp;Explicitly describes vacuum energy as gravitationally â€œfalling outward,â€ generating runaway expansion. This provides the keystone metaphor for the essayâ€™s cosmological section â€” vacuum as a dissipative system exporting its â€œorderâ€ into larger voids.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Philosophical and Cognitive Parallels</p>
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">Anderson, M. (2006). After Phrenology: Neural Reuse and the Interactive Brain. MIT Press.
&nbsp;&nbsp;Argues against modular cognitive theories, emphasizing neural reuse. This parallels Fantâ€™s invocation logic: systems are not self-contained modules but continually invoke higher contexts.</li>
<li class="break-words">Clark, A. (2013). Whatever Next? Predictive Brains, Situated Agents, and the Future of Cognitive Science. Behavioral and Brain Sciences, 36(3), 181â€“204.
&nbsp;&nbsp;Clarkâ€™s predictive processing model shows how cognition depends on minimizing error via external feedback loops. This maps to the essayâ€™s claim that no system is complete internally; predictive brains externalize to their environment.</li>
<li class="break-words">Hohwy, J. (2013). The Predictive Mind. Oxford University Press.
&nbsp;&nbsp;Offers a detailed account of predictive coding as the organizing principle of mind. Serves as a philosophical parallel to Prigogine: cognitive systems maintain order by externalizing uncertainty, mirroring how physical systems externalize entropy.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">That way, the references donâ€™t just sit as a list â€” they trace the escalation from GÃ¶delâ€™s incompleteness â†’ Fantâ€™s null logic â†’ Prigogineâ€™s entropy export â†’ Whittleâ€™s falling outward cosmology â†’ cognitive parallels.</p></div><section class="inline-media-container flex flex-col gap-1"></section><section class="auth-notification flex flex-col gap-1"></section></div><div class="order-first sticky hidden @md/mainview:block top-11 h-0 opacity-0 group-focus-within:opacity-100 group-hover:opacity-100 -mr-[36px] @lg/mainview:-mr-12"><div class="min-h-7 py-4 flex flex-col gap-0.5"><button class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium leading-[normal] cursor-pointer focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed transition-colors duration-100 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 select-none text-fg-secondary hover:text-fg-primary hover:bg-button-ghost-hover disabled:hover:text-fg-secondary disabled:hover:bg-transparent [&amp;_svg]:hover:text-fg-primary h-10 w-10 rounded-full" type="button" aria-label="Edit" data-state="closed"><span style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="stroke-[2] size-4"><path d="M18.25 5.75C16.8693 4.36929 14.6307 4.36929 13.25 5.75L10.125 8.875L5.52404 13.476C4.86236 14.1376 4.45361 15.0104 4.36889 15.9423L4 20.0001L8.0578 19.6311C8.98967 19.5464 9.86234 19.1377 10.524 18.476L18.25 10.75C19.6307 9.36929 19.6307 7.13071 18.25 5.75V5.75Z" stroke="currentColor"></path><path d="M12.5 7.5L16.5 11.5" stroke="currentColor"></path></svg></span></button><button class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium leading-[normal] cursor-pointer focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:cursor-not-allowed t