<h3 dir="auto" class="text-xl">Explanation and Notes</h3>
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Addressing the Shortness Issue</strong>:
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">The previous version was short because it was a placeholder or summary. This expanded version significantly extends each section, particularly the NCL section (2), which now includes a detailed explanation of NCL principles, dual-rail encoding, and the data/null wavefront cycle, as discussed in <em>Computer Science Reconsidered</em> \citep{fant2005}. The essay is now comprehensive, with each section fleshed out to provide depth and context, totaling several pages when compiled.</li>
<li class="break-words">The NCL section includes prerequisites for readers unfamiliar with computation, explaining Boolean logic limitations, asynchronous design, and the role of null states, making it accessible yet rigorous.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Bibliography Fix</strong>:
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">The BibTeX errors arose because the LaTeX file referenced <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">refs.bib</span> while your system used <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">references.bib</span>, and no citations were found due to missing <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\cite</span> commands. This version uses <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibliography{references}</span> to match your <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">references.bib</span> file, and in-text citations (e.g., <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\citep{godel1931}</span>) are added throughout to ensure BibTeX processes correctly.</li>
<li class="break-words">The <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">references.bib</span> file includes all provided references, formatted for compatibility with the <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">plainnat</span> bibliography style.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Incorporating Prior Discussions</strong>:
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">GÃ¶delian Incompleteness</strong>: Expanded with references to \citet{tarski1956} and \citet{nagel1958}, emphasizing self-reference and pluralism.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">NCL</strong>: Detailed explanation of Fantâ€™s framework, including three/four-value logic, dual-rail encoding, and everyday analogues (learnerâ€™s permit, amber light, Matthew 26:29), as per your earlier discussions.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">GOFAI Critiques</strong>: Integrated Andersonâ€™s arguments against rule-based AI, linking to sub-symbolic adaptability \citep{anderson2006, clark2013, hohwy2013}.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Functional Programming</strong>: Expanded with monadic deferral, referencing \citet{wadler1992, turner1979}, and tied to entropy export.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Prigogineâ€™s Dissipative Structures</strong>: Detailed with thermodynamic principles and examples (e.g., Uber, garbage collection), citing \citet{prigogine1984, nicolis1977, schneider2005}.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">RSVP Cosmology</strong>: Incorporates Whittleâ€™s ``falling outward'' \citep{whittle2015}, with RSVPâ€™s entropic relaxation and CMB constraints, referencing \citet{einstein1917, desitter1917, peebles2003, riess1998, perlmutter1999, dodelson2003}.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Law of Superset Entropy</strong>: Implicitly woven into the synthesis, unifying all domains under the idea of exporting or internalizing incompleteness.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Appendix</strong>:
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">The CMB dipole constraints appendix is included verbatim from the previously refined version, using <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ï•</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">Ï•</span></span></span></span> for the scalar field, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Î¥</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Upsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Î¥</span></span></span></span> for the entropic redshift potential, and ensuring all tweaks (e.g., normalization, <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Îµ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\rm int}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">Îµ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3175em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathrm mtight">int</span></span></span><