<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words">The first <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">pdflatex</span> run generates the <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">.aux</span> file, which includes <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibdata{references}</span> and <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibstyle{plainnat}</span>.</li>
<li class="break-words">The <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">bibtex</span> run processes <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">references.bib</span> to create the <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">.bbl</span> file.</li>
<li class="break-words">The subsequent <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">pdflatex</span> runs resolve citations and cross-references.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Troubleshooting BibTeX Errors</strong>:
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">No <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibdata</span> command</strong>: Ensure <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">references.bib</span> is in the same directory as <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">incompleteness.tex</span>. Check that the file is readable and not corrupted (e.g., open it in a text editor to confirm no stray characters).</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">No <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibstyle</span> command</strong>: Verify that <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibliographystyle{plainnat}</span> and <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibliography{references}</span> are present in <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">incompleteness.tex</span> before <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\end{document}</span>.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">File not found</strong>: If BibTeX still fails, try specifying the full path to <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">references.bib</span> in the <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibliography</span> command, e.g., <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibliography{./references}</span>.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Clean build</strong>: Remove auxiliary files (<span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">rm incompleteness.aux incompleteness.bbl incompleteness.blg</span>) and re-run the compilation sequence to avoid stale <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">.aux</span> issues.</li>
</ul>
</li>
