<h3 dir="auto" class="text-xl">Notes</h3>
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Modularity</strong>: The <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\input{appendices}</span> command includes <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">appendices.tex</span> seamlessly, maintaining modularity. You can edit <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">appendices.tex</span> independently without altering <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">incompleteness.tex</span>. If you prefer a single file, you can copy the content of <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">appendices.tex</span> into <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">incompleteness.tex</span> before <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibliographystyle</span>.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Error Fixes</strong>: The BibTeX errors are addressed by ensuring proper placement of <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibliographystyle{plainnat}</span> and <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\bibliography{references}</span>. The previous compilation errors (runaway arguments, undefined <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\references</span>, overfull hboxes, unclosed groups) are fixed in the provided <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">incompleteness.tex</span> via correct citation syntax, <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">\hyphenation</span>, and balanced environments.</li>
